From 712ebae6642bfa7deb70afa6b769e96fa37aa2af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 20:02:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] net: airoha: validate SOE incarnations and delayed
 observations

Allocate non-reused software identities in the built-in skb core so
identities survive provider reprobe and driver module reload. Associate
each programmed SA with its identity and validate initial, cached and
delayed PPE commits against the active incarnation under ppe_lock.

Carry the SA and exact metadata observation in a refcounted skb
extension. This prevents old completions and queued skbs from consuming
metadata for a new SA or a new observation at the same hash, and
preserves all nfmark bits. Allocation or identity exhaustion falls back
to the normal path. Existing hardware drain/quarantine rules remain
necessary; software identities cannot prove that a hardware bypass
pipeline has drained.

Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
